      "attributes": {
        "depth": "explanation"
      },
      "contextualization": {
        "value": "none",
        "evidence": []
      },
      "accuracy": {
        "verdict": "accurate",
        "reason": "Correctly explains that atomic size increases down the group due to the addition of successive electron shells.",
        "errors": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "u8",
      "kind": "CONCEPT",
      "label": "Ionization energy comparison and downward group trend",
      "excerpts": [
        {
          "text": "### 5. **आयनन ऊर्जा (Ionization Energy)**\n- Group 1 से अधिक होती है (क्योंकि 2 इलेक्ट्रॉन निकालना ज़्यादा मुश्किल)\n- ऊपर से नीचे जाने पर **घटती** है",
          "occurrence": 0
        }
      ],
      "attributes": {
        "depth": "explanation"
      },
      "contextualization": {
        "value": "none",
        "evidence": []
      },
      "accuracy": {
        "verdict": "contains_error",
        "reason": "The trends that ionization energy is higher than Group 1 and decreases down the group are correct, but explaining that it is higher because 'removing two electrons is harder' is a conceptual error. Ionization energy refers to removing one electron at a time; first ionization energy is higher in Group 2 than Group 1 because of higher effective nuclear charge, smaller atomic radius, and a completely filled s-subshell.",
        "errors": [
          {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "excerpt_index": 0,
                "quote": "क्योंकि 2 इलेक्ट्रॉन निकालना ज़्यादा मुश्किल"
              }
            ],
            "description": "Ionization energy is defined as the energy required to remove an electron from an isolated neutral gaseous atom. Explaining that Group 2 has higher ionization energy than Group 1 because 'removing 2 electrons is harder' conflates single-electron ionization energy with successive ionizations; the higher first ionization energy is due to smaller atomic size, higher effective nuclear charge, and the stable ns² configuration.",
            "correction": "क्योंकि Group 2 के तत्वों का परमाणु आकार छोटा और प्रभावी नाभिकीय आवेश (effective nuclear charge) अधिक होता है",
            "severity": "minor"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
